 E3 on the next move lost 5.0, and Black's lead was +9.4 again."}, {"turn": 33, "text": "The 12k's H6 took the G6 stone for a capture, yet it lost 7.7 points, its worst move, as the lead dropped from +16.0 to +8.2. The engine wanted F2. Opus 5.5 had just lost 7.5 with E6 on the previous move, so the position was still messy."}, {"turn": 34, "text": "H3 was Opus 5.5's worst move of the game, losing 8.2 points as the lead went from +8.2 to +16.4. The engine's choice was G2. H4 and H5 then lost 6.4 and 6.5 more, and Black's lead stayed above 14 from there."}, {"turn": 51, "text": "Opus 5.5's H1 had lost 5.8 points, lifting Black's lead to +20.3. The 12k's G6 lost exactly 5.8 and sent it back to +14.4, with the engine preferring E2 both times. It was one more exchange of errors, and Black stayed far ahead."}]}, "audit": {"by": "Sonnet 5.5", "verdict": "clean", "reason": "libs.py flood-fills the board pasted into it and prints each group's stones and liberties, flagging groups with two or fewer. count.py takes the dead stones the player names, removes them, and counts area plus komi. Both only read the current position, with no candidate moves scored and no continuations played out.", "stop": false}}